# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Spooky2 preset database — things that must never enter git
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The preset database is a BUILD ARTIFACT, regenerable in ~2-4 minutes with
#   python preset-db/tools/build_db.py --full
# It is 1.1 GB and must never be committed.
preset-db/build/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Rendered page images from the User's Guide. 244 PNGs, ~81 MB, regenerated by
#   python preset-db/tools/extract_guide.py
preset-db/docs/pages/
preset-db/docs/guide_text.md

# Per-batch raw page reads and vision extractions. Provenance evidence, not
# an input: nothing reads them, and KNOWLEDGE.md is the resolved version.
preset-db/docs/notes/

# The user's Spooky2 corpus: 43,397 read-only .txt files, ~300 MB.
# It is not ours to distribute, and it is regenerable from their own install.
Preset Collections/
Preset Collections.zip
Spooky2.zip

# The program's own export of the (encrypted) frequency database.
# 95,583 programs, 17 MB. Deliberately not ingested: it resolves only 2% of the
# programs referenced by presets. See the note in KNOWLEDGE.md section 10b.
DatabaseText.txt

# Copyrighted source material from The Spooky Team.
*.pdf

# Reverse-engineering work in progress on the encrypted databases. The user
# asked for this to be left out entirely.
Prueba-secreta/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# teoria-JD — the user's own local research folder. Never distributable.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Contains material that is not ours and must not be published:
#   * 33 MB export of a Telegram supergroup's full chat history (43,745
#     messages, 897 participants), exported by a third party.
#   * verbatim transcripts of other people's lectures (Nesterov, van Hoven),
#     automatically transcribed and therefore someone's copyrighted speech.
#   * preset archives, PDFs and screenshots belonging to their authors and to
#     other Telegram participants.
#
# Nothing derived from it may be committed either. Knowledge extracted from
# these sources is written up in preset-db/docs/, attributed by source, and
# kept to what is independently checkable. Private notes stay private.
teoria-JD/

# The parser that reads that folder is a local tool, like the other scripts
# under tools/. It has no place in a public repository because its only input
# is the excluded chat export.
teoria-jd-parser.py
jd_*.jsonl
jd_*.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local runtime noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Pi's own session state and skill-registry cache. Not project content.
.atl/

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# The skill is installed under the user's home config, not here, but keep any
# stray local copy out of the repo.
*.local.md